amazing grok
============

Super fast, accurate transcription and real voice conversations with Grok,
on Linux and macOS, using your xAI account (OAuth, no API key needed).

  tap your hotkey once     dictate: words are typed into whatever window
                           has focus as you speak; tap again to stop
  tap it twice quickly     talk to Grok out loud; it answers back, and can
                           search the web and X; tap once to hang up

Getting started

  1. Get the script (Python 3, no packages needed):

       git clone https://github.com/teddytennant/amazing-grok
       ln -s "$PWD/amazing-grok/amazing-grok" ~/.local/bin/amazing-grok

     Linux needs PipeWire (pw-record/pw-play) and wtype (Wayland) or
     xdotool (X11). macOS needs sox: brew install sox

  2. Sign in with your xAI account:

       amazing-grok login

     (Already signed in to Wizard? That session is reused automatically.
     XAI_API_KEY also works.)

  3. Bind a key to `amazing-grok tap`.

     Hyprland:  bind = , Super_R, exec, amazing-grok tap
     sway:      bindsym Super_R exec amazing-grok tap
     macOS:     use skhd, Hammerspoon or Raycast to run `amazing-grok tap`.
                Give your terminal/hotkey app Accessibility permission (for
                typing) and Microphone permission.

  Or run it directly: amazing-grok dictate | talk | stop | status

Options

  Put these in ~/.config/amazing-grok/config (one per line), or set them as
  environment variables:

  AMAZING_GROK_SPEED=1             how fast Grok talks, 0.7 to 2
  AMAZING_GROK_PAUSE_MS=900        how long a pause means you're done talking
                                   (raise it if Grok cuts you off)
  AMAZING_GROK_VOICE=eve           Grok's voice
  AMAZING_GROK_BARGE_IN=1          talk over Grok (use with headphones)
  AMAZING_GROK_LANG=en             language
  AMAZING_GROK_DOUBLE_TAP_MS=350   double-tap window
  AMAZING_GROK_SOURCE=<name>       PipeWire mic to use

Waybar: a custom module with "exec": "amazing-grok json", "signal": 2,
"return-type": "json" shows what's running. Log: $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/amazing-grok/log
